From 10bc50be46ed59c6f82b39d37a4e67c2a1cd1198 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JU <jusamuel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:55:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): command scheduler, data mapper and device
 session (C3)

- CommandScheduler: per-link serial queue (parallel only with full duplex + correlation key),
  priority STOP > CONTROL > INFO > POLL, response matching (key, expect, late guard, legacy first frame),
  timeout/retry for idempotent commands, in-flight cancel keeps link busy, STOP cancels pending START/PAUSE,
  poll skip, link down/up, link-suspect after consecutive timeouts
- DataMapper: DeviceRef/ChannelRef/LogicalDataRef, transform, range/unmapped/parse-error quality,
  order-independent results; LegacyTagIdMapping (TAG_ID=CH<n>) isolated
- DeviceSession: transport -> framer -> scheduler -> stream parser -> mapper -> values; follows link state
- ExchangePattern/ProtocolRole/CommandAction model (PROT code mapping)
- Tests: response-match conflicts M1-M6, STOP/cancel/timeout S1-S7, identifiers D1-D8, session end-to-end
- No server, DB, client, terminal or IPC change

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
